# reach: home against the stop, then three moves across the range under gravity.
# Format: "name = ...", "duration_s = ...", "at <t> <command> [value]", "accept <metric> <op> <limit>".
# Commands go to the firmware over the link (arm, set_pos, stop) or to the environment (set <name> <value>).
# Metrics are judged from the firmware's telemetry and the plant truth, never from firmware internals.
name = reach
duration_s = 16
at 0.2 arm 1
at 5.0 set_pos 0.5
at 8.0 set_pos -0.8
at 11.0 set_pos 1.2
accept homed == 1
accept fault == 0
accept final_err_rad < 0.02
accept max_t_winding_c < 80
accept max_abs_i_a < 4.5
accept link_bad == 0
